## 🔄 EXECUTION STATE MACHINE (MANDATORY)

Define strict states:

IDLE
→ STARTED
→ STEP_EXECUTION
→ AMBIGUITY
→ USER_INPUT_REQUIRED
→ STEP_RESOLVED
→ FLOW_VALIDATED
→ RECORDING
→ COMPLETED
→ ERROR

System must ALWAYS be in one of these states.

---

🧠 STEP INTERPRETER

Convert step text into structured format:

Example:
"click login" → { action: "click", target: "login" }
"enter username" → { action: "input", field: "username" }

Rules:

* "click" → click action
* "enter/type" → input
* "select" → dropdown

NO ML. Pure rule-based parsing.

---

🔍 ELEMENT DETECTION ENGINE (CRITICAL)

Use multi-strategy detection in this priority:

1. Exact visible text
2. Partial text match
3. aria-label
4. placeholder
5. button/input tags
6. XPath fallback

Playwright locators must be used.

---

⚠️ AMBIGUITY HANDLING

CASE 1: Multiple matches

Backend sends:
{
"type": "AMBIGUITY",
"step": "click fund transfer",
"options": [
{ "selector": "...", "position": "top-right" },
{ "selector": "...", "position": "bottom-left" }
]
}

Frontend must:

* Highlight elements in browser
* Show options to user
* Send selected option back

---

❌ NOT FOUND HANDLING

Backend sends:
{
"type": "NOT_FOUND",
"step": "click reports"
}

Frontend must:

* Show error message
* Provide input box
* Allow user to correct text
* Send corrected value

Retry step after correction

---

💾 LEARNING MEMORY

Store mappings locally:

{
"click login": "button#loginBtn"
}

Reuse in future runs before searching again

---

✅ FLOW VALIDATION PHASE (MANDATORY)

* Execute all steps once
* Resolve all ambiguity and missing elements
* If ANY step fails → DO NOT proceed

Only when all steps succeed:
→ Move to RECORDING state

---

🌐 BROWSER EXECUTION

Use Playwright (non-headless)

* Launch browser
* Maintain session
* Handle cookies/tokens automatically

DO NOT use HTTP-only requests

---

📡 NETWORK CAPTURE

Capture via:

1. HAR recording
2. request/response listeners

Store:

* URL
* method
* headers
* payload
* response time

---

📊 TRANSACTION BUILDER

Map steps to transactions:

start_transaction("login")
end_transaction("login")

Naming must be derived from step text

---

📁 OUTPUT FORMAT

Store locally as JSON:

{
"transactions": [],
"network_calls": [],
"metadata": {}
}

